<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  App-level Privacy Manifest, added 2026-08-23. Apple has required this
  for new App Store submissions since spring 2024 for apps that use
  certain "required reason" APIs.

  What's declared here (high confidence, well-established categories):
  - No tracking (LocalSync has no cross-app/cross-site tracking of any
    kind - it's local-first by design).
  - UserDefaults API usage, reason CA92.1 ("access info from the same
    app, or from an App Group it's a member of") - shared_preferences
    reads/writes NSUserDefaults directly for device name, selected
    skin, saved bare-repo path, and IAP unlock state, all first-party,
    never shared outside the app.

  What's NOT independently verified here, flag before submitting:
  device_info_plus and shared_preferences_foundation both already bundle
  their OWN PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy (confirmed present in their pub-cache
  source, 2026-08-23) - Xcode merges those into the app automatically,
  nothing to add for them here. purchases_flutter (RevenueCat) v8.11.0
  did NOT have one found in pub-cache at the same check - if RevenueCat's
  native SDK uses any other required-reason API category (e.g. File
  Timestamp, System Boot Time), that would need its own declaration and
  wasn't checked here. The reliable way to catch anything missed: Xcode
  15+ generates a real Privacy Report at Product > Archive > Distribute
  App, which flags any required-reason API used with no matching
  declaration - run that for real before submitting, don't trust this
  file's completeness on faith.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
